:"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-11-23T18:41:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-23T20:57:49Z","closed_at":"2025-11-23T19:29:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS\n\n### Issue description\n\nI noticed while playing around with 3D meshes that the axes are completely off. When making a instanced mesh with a plane mesh, the plane mesh is along the xz plane but the values that you change to set the size of the plane mesh correspond to the xy plane, which doesn't make much sense. Funnily setting the center offset of the plane mesh is correct axis wise. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake a new scene, make a MeshInstance3D, add a plane mesh to the MeshInstance3D, change the values for size, and notice it's not on the right axes. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMake a new scene, make a MeshInstance3D, add a plane mesh to the MeshInstance3D, change the values for size, and notice it's not on the right axes. This is like 3 steps, so I didn't bother with an MRP, and it takes like 10 seconds to reproduce max. ","closed_by":{"login":"WhoIsRam","id":114957050,"node_id":"U_kgDOBtoa-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114957050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhoIsRam","html_url":"https://github.com/WhoIsRam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhoIsRam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhoIsRam/following{/other_user}","